   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\">\r\n<div style=\"font-size:12pt;color:#000000;font-family:Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif\" dir=\"ltr\">\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p style=\"font-family:Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif,EmojiFont,&quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;,NotoColorEmoji,&quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;,&quot;Android Emoji&quot;,EmojiSymbols;font-size:16px\">\r\nHey guys,</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-family:Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif,EmojiFont,&quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;,NotoColorEmoji,&quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;,&quot;Android Emoji&quot;,EmojiSymbols;font-size:16px\">\r\n<br>\r\n</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-family:Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif,EmojiFont,&quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;,NotoColorEmoji,&quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;,&quot;Android Emoji&quot;,EmojiSymbols;font-size:16px\">\r\nWhat determines the tolerance value (Q) in the convergence computation using partial Procrustes superimposition? Is it an arbitrary number? I learned that &#39;Morpho&#39; provides an option to alter this quantity: procSym (tol = ) and if I have understood this correctly,\r\n then this is apparently critical when dealing with an increasing number of sliding semi landmarks. </p>\r\n<p style=\"font-family:Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif,EmojiFont,&quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;,NotoColorEmoji,&quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;,&quot;Android Emoji&quot;,EmojiSymbols;font-size:16px\">\r\n<br>\r\n</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-family:Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif,EmojiFont,&quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;,NotoColorEmoji,&quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;,&quot;Android Emoji&quot;,EmojiSymbols;font-size:16px\">\r\nCheers,</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-family:Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif,EmojiFont,&quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;,NotoColorEmoji,&quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;,&quot;Android Emoji&quot;,EmojiSymbols;font-size:16px\">\r\nMohamad</p>\r\n<br>\r\n<p></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<u></u>\r\n\r\n<br>\r\n<br>\r\n<br>\r\n<br>\r\n<br>\r\n<br>\r\n<br>\r\n<br>\r\nNär du har kontakt med oss på Uppsala universitet med e-post så innebär det att vi behandlar dina personuppgifter. För att läsa mer om hur vi gör det kan du läsa här: <a href=\"http://www.uu.se/om-uu/dataskydd-personuppgifter/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.uu.se/om-uu/dataskydd-personuppgifter/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792485171971000&amp;usg=AOvVaw00sSb-JWOK84-4Yc7oTHQX\">http://www.uu.se/om-uu/dataskydd-personuppgifter/</a>\r\n<br>\r\n<br>\r\nE-mailing Uppsala University means that we will process your personal data. For more information on how this is performed, please read here: <a href=\"http://www.uu.se/en/about-uu/data-protection-policy\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.uu.se/en/about-uu/data-protection-policy&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792485171971000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0YtIq2b-pT9o0-a2r2C0lG\">http://www.uu.se/en/about-uu/data-protection-policy</a>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n"
    ]
